  :coscientist/subject "Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct Q4_K_M (llama.cpp's default download quant; token_embd Q5_0, output Q8_0, attn_v Q8_0 in layers 0-1 and Q5_0 after, ffn_down Q6_K in 12 layers and Q4_K in 12). Two blockers: (1) the embedding kernel had no legacy 32-block arm -> embed_iq4xs.comp -DB32=<2|3|6|7> (Q4_0/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1 as ggml-quants.c); first build wrote only blocks 0-23 of 28 because the IQ4_XS early return (blocks = cols/256) was still in front of the arm; (2) the dense kdot metas were typed from blk.0 for every layer -> attn_v read as Q8_0 and ffn_down as Q6_K from layer 2 -> NaN (3-layer debug guest: dv 55 NaN of 128 while a standalone kdot on the same tensor was exact 2.6e-6). Fix: metas per [phase shape, role, distinct type], a per-layer type signature index, the shared layer function derives sig from its weight base (a 6th parameter hits the native ABI arity :kotoba.error/max-parameters; per-layer meta buffers were 720 WRITEs / 150 KB, over the literal budget) and varying roles select with an (if (= sig k)) chain. K16: fn 13/13 argmax, x rel 3.2e-6..1.4e-5, 17.2 ms/token; adaptive 4/4 rows B=1 16.24 / B=4 19.25 ms/step. Controls: Q8_0 file 4/4 18.56 with the new generator; Nex anv guest byte-identical"
